{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_vii", "label": "Article VII \u2014 Attribution", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_x", "label": "Article X \u2014 Reputation is not authority", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_stage", "label": "Stage 27 \u2014 Model provenance and task routing (planned, not started)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Planned, not built. A claim extraction over a long transcript needs a frontier model with a large context; deciding whether one quoted sentence supports one claim does not, and a 7B model on a local GPU could do that volume work for nothing. Today the ledger cannot tell the two apart, so it offers every task to everyone."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_not_a_scoring_change", "label": "The model is provenance and routing; it never touches a score", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dangerous reading is \"work by a better model is better work\", which Article XI, Invariant 8 and Invariant 7 all forbid \u2014 and a model name is a weaker signal than either, self-declared besides. It may decide who is offered a task and how often that work is audited; it may never change a probability, a state or a trace, and the scoring configs do not learn the field exists. Acceptance test 4 checks the goldens rather than trusting the reading."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_declared_not_fact", "label": "A declared model is a claim about itself, not a fact", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An assistant says what it is and nothing verifies it, so the record stores and shows it as declared. A local 7B claiming to be a frontier model gets frontier tasks and fails its audits, which is what audits are for. UNKNOWN is the default tier and never an error \u2014 a fact about config/models.yml, not about the model \u2014 and UNKNOWN is offered SMALL work only, the same conservative reading the ledger applies wherever it does not know something."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_software_is_junk_today", "label": "The envelope's `software` field exists and is unusable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Of 600 sampled contributions only 173 carry `software` at all; model_id was \"oauth\" 93 times, \"unknown\" 37, \"none\" 5 and a real identifier 26. The OAuth connect path writes a connection method into the field that should hold a model, nothing validates it, and no projection, index, query, page or routing reads it. An honest unknown is worth more than a wrong answer \u2014 the same rule the scoring model follows for INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_single_model_dependence", "label": "single_model_dependence on the weaknesses page", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The honest use of the field: a claim whose evidence rests entirely on work by one declared model, or entirely on UNKNOWN declarations, is a real weakness. Not to discount the work, but to say plainly what it rests on (Article XXII)."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_not_a_scoring_change", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_declared_not_fact", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_software_is_junk_today", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_single_model_dependence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-27-model-provenance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_27_model_provenance_stage", "target": "app_services_tasks_lease_lease", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_fi